1
00:00:06,454 --> 00:00:11,719
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is Chulla Sunyata Sutta, Manjumanikaya 121.

2
00:00:14,901 --> 00:00:15,822
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus have I heard.

3
00:00:17,743 --> 00:00:26,771
[SPEAKER_00]: On one occasion, the Blessed One was living at Savatthi, at the place of Megara's mother.

4
00:00:27,131 --> 00:00:32,115
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, in the evening, having emerged from seclusion, the Venerable Ananda approached the Blessed One.

5
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:36,768
[SPEAKER_00]: Having approached the Blessed One, having paid respects, he sat down to one side.

6
00:00:37,828 --> 00:00:49,111
[SPEAKER_00]: Sitting down at one side, the Venerable Ānanda said to this Blessed One, There was this one occasion when the Blessed One was living among the Sākyans, a Sākyan town called Nāgāraka.

7
00:00:50,251 --> 00:00:53,252
[SPEAKER_00]: There, Bhante, in the presence of the Blessed One, this was heard by me.

8
00:00:54,633 --> 00:00:59,734
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, Ānanda, I often dwell with the place of emptiness.

9
00:01:01,583 --> 00:01:05,605
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I'm not sure, Bhante, if this was well heard, well grasped, well attended, well remembered by me.

10
00:01:06,906 --> 00:01:10,809
[SPEAKER_00]: Certainly, Ananda, this was well heard, well grasped, well attended, well remembered by you.

11
00:01:12,169 --> 00:01:15,211
[SPEAKER_00]: Both before and now, I often dwell with the place of emptiness.

12
00:01:16,772 --> 00:01:29,400
[SPEAKER_00]: Ananda, just as this place of Megara's mother is empty of elephants, cattle and mares, empty of gold and silver, empty of crowds, women, men, there is this non-emptiness.

13
00:01:31,337 --> 00:01:33,898
[SPEAKER_00]: Namely, the oneness dependent on the bhikkhu-saṅgha.

14
00:01:35,018 --> 00:01:43,080
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point here is the presence of the negative.

15
00:01:43,241 --> 00:01:46,962
[SPEAKER_00]: And by that mean... that's basically what emptiness means.

16
00:01:47,022 --> 00:01:49,822
[SPEAKER_00]: Presence of emptiness is presence of certain absences.

17
00:01:50,783 --> 00:01:58,465
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in this particular case, the Mīgara's mother palace is empty.

18
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:03,907
[SPEAKER_00]: It's absent of elephants, cattle, mares, gold, silver, crowds, women, men.

19
00:02:05,048 --> 00:02:08,191
[SPEAKER_00]: But what is not empty of is the group of the bhikkhu-saṅgha.

20
00:02:10,112 --> 00:02:23,284
[SPEAKER_00]: So, attending to that which is absent as a uniform basis can be seen as a uniform phenomena, as a single phenomena.

21
00:02:23,444 --> 00:02:26,947
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it's meant by oneness, basically, one-pointedness.

22
00:02:28,105 --> 00:02:34,068
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind is established upon a single more general phenomena, in this case, the negative phenomena of absence.

23
00:02:39,471 --> 00:02:42,292
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the oneness dependent on the bhikkhu-saṅgha.

24
00:02:45,794 --> 00:02:53,378
[SPEAKER_00]: In just this way, Ananda, bhikkhu not attending to the perception of village, not attending to the perception of people,

25
00:02:55,533 --> 00:03:11,136
[SPEAKER_00]: So, a bhikkhu can surmount the perception of the village, perception of people, by having his mind established on the perception of the forest.

26
00:03:11,856 --> 00:03:18,017
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, even when he's not in the forest, he could maintain that perception.

27
00:03:19,978 --> 00:03:21,978
[SPEAKER_00]: So, although that perception will be absent,

28
00:03:22,723 --> 00:03:28,544
[SPEAKER_00]: When he is among people or in the village, his mind still remains established upon that oneness.

29
00:03:33,585 --> 00:03:34,465
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what it says here.

30
00:03:34,525 --> 00:03:42,126
[SPEAKER_00]: His mind jumps onto, it is clear about, remains with, inclines towards the perception of the forest.

31
00:03:42,146 --> 00:03:50,188
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's not some sort of, like, a mystical nimitta or whatever you want to call it, upon which his perception is established.

32
00:03:50,268 --> 00:03:51,388
[SPEAKER_00]: It's actually the clarity

33
00:03:52,604 --> 00:04:06,370
[SPEAKER_00]: of the of the of the peripheral awareness of his experience, while he was in the forest, still remains present, because his mind is established upon it, even when he comes out of the forest.

34
00:04:07,071 --> 00:04:20,357
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he uses the perceptions of the forest, he uses the perceptions of the forest, to to maintain his mind established upon that oneness, even when he leaves the forest.

35
00:04:23,645 --> 00:04:24,825
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he understands thus.

36
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:31,387
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever anxiety there might be dependent on the perception of the village, those are not present here.

37
00:04:32,288 --> 00:04:42,771
[SPEAKER_00]: Because his mind refuses to descend from the more general perception of the the mood of the forest that he dwells in, refused to descend onto the perceptions of the village.

38
00:04:42,931 --> 00:04:46,712
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he never gets pulled by them.

39
00:04:47,492 --> 00:04:53,014
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means any anxiety that can arise on account of the perceptions in the village, does not bother him.

40
00:05:03,244 --> 00:05:09,008
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever anxiety there might be dependent on the perception of people, those anxieties are not present here.

41
00:05:09,968 --> 00:05:18,093
[SPEAKER_00]: There is only this much anxiety, this much disturbance, namely based upon the oneness dependent on the perception of the forest.

42
00:05:19,274 --> 00:05:31,902
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if something were to happen to that forest, he's still liable to a certain amount of disturbance, some certain amount of discomfort arising on account of it, because that's where his mind is established.

43
00:05:33,369 --> 00:05:34,050
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

44
00:05:34,270 --> 00:05:37,412
[SPEAKER_00]: Having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the perception of the village.

45
00:05:37,572 --> 00:05:40,595
[SPEAKER_00]: Having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the perception of people.

46
00:05:41,215 --> 00:05:42,796
[SPEAKER_00]: There is only this non-emptiness.

47
00:05:43,517 --> 00:05:46,059
[SPEAKER_00]: The oneness dependent on the perception of the forest.

48
00:05:46,459 --> 00:05:47,240
[SPEAKER_00]: That is not empty.

49
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:49,502
[SPEAKER_00]: But, he dwells empty.

50
00:05:51,440 --> 00:06:00,364
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it can be seen here, it's not some sort of mystical emptiness, mystical reality behind the appearances.

51
00:06:00,584 --> 00:06:03,185
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a presence of absence.

52
00:06:04,145 --> 00:06:10,908
[SPEAKER_00]: In this case, absence of unwholesome environment or environment that's less conducive for practice.

53
00:06:11,428 --> 00:06:13,909
[SPEAKER_00]: Absence of people, absence of village.

54
00:06:14,935 --> 00:06:28,399
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even when the monk goes for pinnapad, goes back into the village, his mind can still remain established upon the absence of the village, as in, he's still rooted in his presence in the forest.

55
00:06:29,039 --> 00:06:31,500
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what it says here.

56
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:39,942
[SPEAKER_00]: He says he has understood the emptiness of the perception of the village, and the emptiness of the perception of the people, and the non-emptiness that is present,

57
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:48,557
[SPEAKER_00]: Is the... the oneness that's dependent upon the perceptions of the forest.

58
00:06:50,659 --> 00:06:57,844
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, on account of whatever it's not there, the absence I've been talking about, he sees it as it empty.

59
00:06:58,645 --> 00:07:02,288
[SPEAKER_00]: And whatever remains, he understands it as this is present.

60
00:07:03,248 --> 00:07:09,633
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even when he's in the village, the perceptions of the forest are present for him, because that's where his mind is established.

61
00:07:10,755 --> 00:07:23,883
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the particular perception of the village that he has, they do not reach, they do not change the background of his mood, of that peripheral mindfulness and awareness, which is still rooted in the perceptions of the forest.

62
00:07:24,283 --> 00:07:28,285
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how he's not disturbed by anything that he sees in the village or hears in the village.

63
00:07:31,807 --> 00:07:38,311
[SPEAKER_00]: And then it says, and in this way, Ananda, there is this authentic, undistorted, clear entry into the emptiness.

64
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:53,053
[SPEAKER_00]: Furthermore, Ananda, a bhikkhu not attending to the perception of the village, not attending to the perception of people, not attending to the perception of the forest, attends to the oneness dependent on the perception of the earth.

65
00:07:53,594 --> 00:07:54,975
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he goes even higher.

66
00:07:56,016 --> 00:08:02,744
[SPEAKER_00]: After his mind has been established upon the perception of the forest, he realizes that he can still be disturbed on the account of that.

67
00:08:13,406 --> 00:08:15,809
[SPEAKER_00]: He realized that he can still be disturbed on account of it.

68
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,511
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then he goes further.

69
00:08:18,252 --> 00:08:21,656
[SPEAKER_00]: But in this case, he doesn't actually go anywhere.

70
00:08:22,697 --> 00:08:30,306
[SPEAKER_00]: He discerns what is even more general in the perception of the village, in the perception of the people, in the perception of the forest.

71
00:08:31,204 --> 00:08:52,944
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the perception of the solidity of the phenomena, the aspect, the element of Earth, which means it's the most general presence of phenomena, which doesn't really require you to be in any particular place, but simply to discern the aspect of solidity, the aspect of resistance of things that appear through your senses.

72
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:18,999
[SPEAKER_00]: And the reason why this is, why the mind can get established upon this, is because anything solid in the world, anything, any environment that you live in, already partakes in the environment of Earth as a whole.

73
00:09:21,691 --> 00:09:37,353
[SPEAKER_00]: The forest, the mountain, the island, the continent, earth as a whole, the element of earth is there, present all the way down into the most particular aspects of some particular village, of such and such name, with such and such people.

74
00:09:40,054 --> 00:09:52,824
[SPEAKER_00]: So, his mind then clarifies and discerns that phenomenon of earth that is contained in all the more particular perceptions of the forest, of the village, of the people.

75
00:09:53,835 --> 00:09:56,436
[SPEAKER_00]: So, through the element of earth, he discerns the actual earth.

76
00:10:19,295 --> 00:10:23,679
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh... that earth is equally present in anything else that appears on that earth.

77
00:10:23,899 --> 00:10:31,185
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there... he doesn't... he's not bothered by any, eh... mountains, forests, different environments, jumps and creeks.

78
00:10:31,265 --> 00:10:33,867
[SPEAKER_00]: Everything is stretched and even in terms of its presence.

79
00:10:34,688 --> 00:10:41,073
[SPEAKER_00]: In terms of his... his, eh... mind being established upon the oneness dependent upon the perception of earth.

80
00:10:42,835 --> 00:10:43,716
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands thus.

81
00:10:44,895 --> 00:10:48,817
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever anxiety there might be dependent on the perception of people, those are not present here.

82
00:10:49,258 --> 00:10:53,080
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever anxiety there might be dependent on the perception of forest, those are not present here.

83
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:58,843
[SPEAKER_00]: There is only this much anxiety, namely, the oneness dependent on the perception of earth.

84
00:10:59,103 --> 00:10:59,804
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

85
00:11:00,284 --> 00:11:03,286
[SPEAKER_00]: Having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the perception of people.

86
00:11:03,726 --> 00:11:06,788
[SPEAKER_00]: Having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the perception of the forest.

87
00:11:07,568 --> 00:11:11,251
[SPEAKER_00]: There is only this non-emptiness, namely, the oneness dependent on the perception of earth.

88
00:11:12,171 --> 00:11:13,612
[SPEAKER_00]: So, by establishing his mind,

89
00:11:15,111 --> 00:11:24,536
[SPEAKER_00]: Upon the most general perception of earth as a whole, he's thus empty of all the other perceptions.

90
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:35,082
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, on account of whatever it's not there, he sees it as empty.

91
00:11:35,882 --> 00:11:38,904
[SPEAKER_00]: And whatever remains, he understands it as this is present.

92
00:11:40,434 --> 00:11:45,255
[SPEAKER_00]: And in this way, Ananda, there is this authentic, undistorted, clear entry into emptiness.

93
00:11:51,956 --> 00:12:09,740
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then it goes further, following the same principle, going for the next, even higher, establishment of mind, which is still based upon the perception on the level of the peripheral mindfulness, and that is the perception of the domain of the infinite space,

94
00:12:10,863 --> 00:12:20,466
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, even the element of earth, even the solidity aspect of things that appear, already requires a negative phenomenon of space.

95
00:12:21,667 --> 00:12:27,629
[SPEAKER_00]: Space is discerned through that appearance, which means space is always there whenever there is appearance.

96
00:12:27,829 --> 00:12:28,429
[SPEAKER_00]: Quiet, boy.

97
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:39,913
[SPEAKER_00]: Space is always there whenever there is appearance, which means that space can also be discerned as that which is in common to absolutely everything that has a nature to appear.

98
00:12:40,472 --> 00:12:47,714
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it's called the infinite space.

99
00:12:50,035 --> 00:12:57,578
[SPEAKER_00]: So, his mind develops clarity about, inclines towards that perception of the domain of the infinite space.

100
00:12:57,938 --> 00:13:01,879
[SPEAKER_00]: It actually properly discerns it within things that are present.

101
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:09,902
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands thus, whatever anxiety there might be dependent on the perception of the forest, dependent on the perception of earth,

102
00:13:10,645 --> 00:13:11,645
[SPEAKER_00]: Those are not present here.

103
00:13:12,905 --> 00:13:18,507
[SPEAKER_00]: There is only this much anxiety, the oneness, dependent on the perception of the domain of infinite space.

104
00:13:21,627 --> 00:13:28,989
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, he understands that having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the perception of forest, arrived at this perception, empty of the perception of earth.

105
00:13:29,009 --> 00:13:33,750
[SPEAKER_00]: There is the non-emptiness, the perception of the domain of the infinite space.

106
00:13:37,777 --> 00:13:42,479
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he goes further, not attending to the perception of Earth, not attending to the perception of the domain of infinite space.

107
00:13:42,979 --> 00:13:49,882
[SPEAKER_00]: He then attends to even greater general phenomenon.

108
00:13:50,062 --> 00:13:54,603
[SPEAKER_00]: Even more peripheral, even more subtle, even more fundamental.

109
00:13:55,744 --> 00:13:57,905
[SPEAKER_00]: And that is simply consciousness.

110
00:13:58,825 --> 00:14:01,906
[SPEAKER_00]: As we mentioned in other talks, consciousness means presence of phenomena.

111
00:14:02,686 --> 00:14:03,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Presence of things.

112
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:06,748
[SPEAKER_00]: The aspect of presence is what consciousness is.

113
00:14:07,793 --> 00:14:13,496
[SPEAKER_00]: Usually, people think consciousness is in them, and because of that, they think things appear for them.

114
00:14:13,716 --> 00:14:14,557
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's not the case.

115
00:14:14,677 --> 00:14:17,398
[SPEAKER_00]: Consciousness is out there with the phenomenon, peripherally.

116
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:20,740
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't attend the consciousness.

117
00:14:22,822 --> 00:14:31,967
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can learn how to non-directly attend the peripheral nature of whatever is present.

118
00:14:32,785 --> 00:14:39,811
[SPEAKER_00]: And by doing so, that's how you develop emptiness of what's... what's in front of you, as we just read through this sutta.

119
00:14:40,471 --> 00:14:58,987
[SPEAKER_00]: So, by not attending to the perception of the forest that the monk is in, by not attending to the perception of the earth that the forest is in, that the monk is in, by not attending to the perception of the infinite space that the earth is in, that the forest is in, that the monk is in, he attends to the perception of the... just...

120
00:15:00,487 --> 00:15:02,470
[SPEAKER_00]: Plain, simple, presence.

121
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:07,776
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't matter what is present, how big it is, big or small, far or near, presence is there.

122
00:15:08,277 --> 00:15:10,780
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all that he discerns, peripherally.

123
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:15,907
[SPEAKER_00]: That's all that he that he becomes clear about and his mind gets established upon.

124
00:15:16,907 --> 00:15:26,638
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what means the infinity of consciousness, the infinite consciousness, as in the presence discerning its nature, not bound to the any particular manifestation of it.

125
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:29,321
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, it's not a mystification.

126
00:15:29,341 --> 00:15:35,809
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just a simple structural discernment in regard to things that are present.

127
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:55,648
[SPEAKER_00]: So, by emptying himself of the perceptions of himself, of the perceptions of the Bhikkhu Saṅgha, of the perceptions of the forest, of the perceptions of the earth, of the perceptions of the infinite space, infinite spaces, he then arrives at the perceptions of the infinite consciousness.

128
00:15:57,792 --> 00:15:58,492
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

129
00:15:58,893 --> 00:16:04,536
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever disturbance there might be dependent on perception of Earth, perception of infinite space, it's not present here.

130
00:16:04,776 --> 00:16:07,538
[SPEAKER_00]: Only the disturbance dependent on the perception of consciousness.

131
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:17,164
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he goes even further, surmounting infinite space, surmounting the infinite consciousness.

132
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:20,001
[SPEAKER_00]: ...attends the perception of the nothingness.

133
00:16:20,101 --> 00:16:26,686
[SPEAKER_00]: And nothingness is the negative in regard to the... that very, very general and subtle consciousness.

134
00:16:27,487 --> 00:16:39,555
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once the the perceptions of forest, the perceptions of oneself, the perceptions of the forest, the perceptions of earth, the perceptions of infinite space, the perceptions of infinite consciousness, the negative to that is nothing.

135
00:16:39,675 --> 00:16:42,237
[SPEAKER_00]: As I said, consciousness is there

136
00:16:42,632 --> 00:16:48,614
[SPEAKER_00]: With the appearance, which means whenever there is appearance, there is presence of that which has appeared, which is what appearance is, which means there is consciousness.

137
00:16:49,154 --> 00:16:54,055
[SPEAKER_00]: The infinity of the consciousness is the nature of that appearance, the nature of the presence of the appearance.

138
00:16:55,556 --> 00:17:03,198
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means, whenever there is something, that something can also be nothing, as in the possibility of it to cease, to not be.

139
00:17:04,038 --> 00:17:07,239
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what the mind discerns then, the nothingness.

140
00:17:07,919 --> 00:17:10,360
[SPEAKER_00]: The absence of this current presence,

141
00:17:11,365 --> 00:17:18,429
[SPEAKER_00]: As we said, when we open up in reading the sutta about the village, the empty of certain things.

142
00:17:19,790 --> 00:17:20,710
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's the negative.

143
00:17:21,451 --> 00:17:33,117
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in this case, the most subtle infinity of consciousness that's seen as a general peripheral phenomena, even that can be surmounted, because even that is something.

144
00:17:33,998 --> 00:17:35,859
[SPEAKER_00]: Although it's very subtle, it's still something.

145
00:17:36,359 --> 00:17:37,320
[SPEAKER_00]: And when there is something,

146
00:17:39,251 --> 00:17:42,993
[SPEAKER_00]: Its possibility is to be nothing, as in to cease, to disappear.

147
00:17:43,133 --> 00:17:51,999
[SPEAKER_00]: So, although there is the present consciousness, the more greater perception, in terms of the peripheral development, is the perception of nothing, nothingness.

148
00:17:55,682 --> 00:18:03,527
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then he understands that there is only anxiety left, dependent upon the perception of the domain of nothingness.

149
00:18:06,598 --> 00:18:16,643
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he goes even further, not attending to perception of the infinite consciousness, perception of the domain of nothingness, he attends to the perception of the domain of the neither perception nor perception.

150
00:18:17,163 --> 00:18:26,248
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even that domain of nothingness is a negative in regard to something, which is, in that case, the domain of the infinite consciousness.

151
00:18:27,128 --> 00:18:27,608
[SPEAKER_00]: And, eh...

152
00:18:28,809 --> 00:18:35,092
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even that domain of nothingness, as peripheral as it is, as negative as it is, as subtle as it is, it's still perceived.

153
00:18:36,417 --> 00:18:37,078
[SPEAKER_00]: To an extent.

154
00:18:37,839 --> 00:18:39,661
[SPEAKER_00]: And now, that's what the monk realizes.

155
00:18:40,241 --> 00:18:44,747
[SPEAKER_00]: He realizes that even such a subtle thing, it's still perceived.

156
00:18:44,927 --> 00:18:52,616
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in order to go even higher, even more generally, even more peripherally, he now needs to surmount the perception.

157
00:18:54,074 --> 00:18:55,935
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not anymore about what's being perceived.

158
00:18:56,175 --> 00:19:02,397
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, he's going beyond the fact that there is a perception of any kind, of presences or absences.

159
00:19:02,417 --> 00:19:02,957
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter.

160
00:19:02,977 --> 00:19:03,757
[SPEAKER_00]: Perception is there.

161
00:19:03,837 --> 00:19:07,138
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what he's surmounting in his in his next effort.

162
00:19:07,578 --> 00:19:08,738
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he develops clarity.

163
00:19:09,219 --> 00:19:10,439
[SPEAKER_00]: He develops understanding.

164
00:19:10,979 --> 00:19:16,821
[SPEAKER_00]: He develops oneness dependent upon the perception of the domain of the neither perception or no perception.

165
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:20,310
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he starts mounting his own perception.

166
00:19:20,810 --> 00:19:29,732
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why even this sutta says that he develops clarity about it, which means it's not some sort of mystical step-by-step entering to some transcendental states.

167
00:19:29,892 --> 00:19:36,954
[SPEAKER_00]: It's understanding of the fundamental nature, structural nature of presence of things, of phenomena.

168
00:19:38,274 --> 00:19:44,755
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is the one-by-one order of that understanding, because the structure is ordered.

169
00:19:45,803 --> 00:19:54,820
[SPEAKER_00]: There is a particular thing, then there is more general, more general, more general, up to the point of surmounting the consciousness, surmounting the nothingness, surmounting the neither perception nor perception.

170
00:19:56,087 --> 00:20:05,109
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whenever the Buddha spoke about this in the past, about the various Samanas and Brahmanas that developed this, it's not that they had some mystical experience that they would amount to this.

171
00:20:05,169 --> 00:20:05,329
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

172
00:20:05,609 --> 00:20:07,949
[SPEAKER_00]: They actually developed the understanding of the phenomena.

173
00:20:08,449 --> 00:20:20,992
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why when the Buddha became an Arahant, when he became enlightened, when he was encouraged by the Brahma to go and teach, when he begged him to do so because people might benefit from it,

174
00:20:22,142 --> 00:20:27,994
[SPEAKER_00]: The first person he wanted to go back and teach was his previous teacher, who was teaching the basis of neither perception nor perception.

175
00:20:29,557 --> 00:20:32,059
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Buddha wasn't doing that out of some sort of gratitude.

176
00:20:32,099 --> 00:20:37,701
[SPEAKER_00]: He was doing because that person would have need absolutely minimal amount of instruction.

177
00:20:37,761 --> 00:20:37,961
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

178
00:20:37,981 --> 00:20:42,063
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you could see how far has his mind been developed beforehand.

179
00:20:42,484 --> 00:20:52,909
[SPEAKER_00]: He has developed the understanding of the phenomena, surpassing the consciousness, the infinite space, surpassing the nature of perception, which means he had very very little dust in his eyes, as the Buddha said.

180
00:20:53,745 --> 00:20:55,125
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why I wanted to go and teach him.

181
00:20:55,706 --> 00:20:59,567
[SPEAKER_00]: But, as it turns out, he died beforehand, and you could understand him why.

182
00:20:59,667 --> 00:21:01,888
[SPEAKER_00]: It was such a... it would have said, oh, it's his great loss.

183
00:21:02,428 --> 00:21:04,549
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he would have understood dhamma in a finger snap.

184
00:21:04,849 --> 00:21:10,891
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he already done all the work.

185
00:21:11,631 --> 00:21:15,633
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once the mind gets established upon the domain of neither perception or no perception,

186
00:21:17,108 --> 00:21:23,231
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the monk will understand that there is only that level of disturbance left, which means it is virtually almost nothing.

187
00:21:23,852 --> 00:21:26,333
[SPEAKER_00]: But, there is still more to go.

188
00:21:26,533 --> 00:21:40,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Following that structural development of the peripheral domain, bhikkhu not attending to the perception of the domain of nothingness, not attending to the perception of the domain of neither perception nor perception, attends to the oneness dependent on the signless composure of the mind.

189
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:45,723
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's where even perceiving the neither perception nor perception has ceased.

190
00:21:47,256 --> 00:21:53,338
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's really... well, there is no room for movement there, for the movement of the mind, for the movement of the perception.

191
00:21:54,698 --> 00:21:57,959
[SPEAKER_00]: And he understands that there is only disturbance left to that extent.

192
00:22:18,019 --> 00:22:19,310
[SPEAKER_00]: Once he, once he fully...

193
00:22:28,208 --> 00:22:39,831
[SPEAKER_00]: Furthermore, Ananda Abhikū, not attending to the perception of the domain of nothingness, not attending to the perception of the domain of neither perception nor perception, attends to the oneness dependent on the signless composure of the mind.

194
00:22:40,611 --> 00:22:44,632
[SPEAKER_00]: His mind jumps onto, it's clear about, remains with, inclines towards the signless composure of the mind.

195
00:22:44,832 --> 00:22:46,172
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, he understands thus.

196
00:22:47,132 --> 00:22:49,033
[SPEAKER_00]: This signless composure of the mind is determined.

197
00:22:50,053 --> 00:22:50,893
[SPEAKER_00]: It is intended.

198
00:22:52,094 --> 00:22:52,794
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands.

199
00:22:53,114 --> 00:22:57,035
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever is determined, it is impermanent and subject to cessation.

200
00:22:57,982 --> 00:23:09,550
[SPEAKER_00]: Which means that this monk was already at least a sotāpanna, because understanding that saṅkharas are impermanent, it's pretty much the insight of an ārya sāvaka.

201
00:23:10,131 --> 00:23:11,231
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in order to

202
00:23:13,214 --> 00:23:42,027
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course, that doesn't mean that the mind cannot be developed by someone who is not an Ārya Sāvaka, but surmounting neither perception nor perception, that is reserved only for an Ārya Sāvaka, only for somebody with the right view, because, as it became obvious, there is no perception there, in a sense of the mind has been unified, surmounting the nature of perception, but the understanding of that, of that place, can take, can take, sorry, the understanding of that establishment can take place reflexively,

203
00:23:43,297 --> 00:23:51,004
[SPEAKER_00]: Whereby, when the mind has developed that clarity, the mind could realize, well, as clear as this is,

204
00:23:52,070 --> 00:23:54,932
[SPEAKER_00]: As subtle as this is, it is still determined.

205
00:23:55,433 --> 00:24:16,890
[SPEAKER_00]: It's determined by the perception, by the domain of perception, which in itself is determined by the domain of infinite consciousness, which in itself is determined by the domain of the infinite space, which in itself is determined by the domain of the earth, which in itself is determined by the domain of any more... any further particular perception, such as perception in the forest, perception in the village, and so on.

206
00:24:17,905 --> 00:24:19,686
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he understands whatever is determined.

207
00:24:19,806 --> 00:24:21,126
[SPEAKER_00]: As such, it is impermanent.

208
00:24:21,686 --> 00:24:23,607
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he penetrates that state with wisdom.

209
00:24:25,287 --> 00:24:32,929
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's... that's how there is absolutely no room in that structure of the arising... arising phenomena, arising experience as a whole.

210
00:24:32,949 --> 00:24:39,031
[SPEAKER_00]: There is absolutely no room that hasn't been... that hasn't been pervaded with that understanding.

211
00:24:39,071 --> 00:24:41,212
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he's surmounted everything and then what's left?

212
00:24:43,390 --> 00:24:45,511
[SPEAKER_00]: Surmounted even that, through his own understanding.

213
00:24:45,711 --> 00:24:48,551
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's absolutely... there's absolutely nothing left.

214
00:24:50,532 --> 00:24:57,933
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says, knowing this, seeing this, for him, the mind is liberated from the taint of sensuality, from the taint of being, from the taint of ignorance.

215
00:24:58,314 --> 00:25:04,095
[SPEAKER_00]: There's absolutely nowhere for those things to remain hidden under things that haven't been upturned.

216
00:25:06,941 --> 00:25:09,203
[SPEAKER_00]: When it is liberated, there is knowledge, it is liberated.

217
00:25:09,263 --> 00:25:12,385
[SPEAKER_00]: Birth is destroyed, holy life has been lived, what should be done has been done.

218
00:25:12,925 --> 00:25:16,208
[SPEAKER_00]: So, again, I don't think it has to repeat this.

219
00:25:16,528 --> 00:25:20,831
[SPEAKER_00]: These are not some transcendental meditative experiences.

220
00:25:20,851 --> 00:25:23,013
[SPEAKER_00]: They're meditative in a sense of they're reflexive.

221
00:25:23,934 --> 00:25:28,037
[SPEAKER_00]: The mind develops clarity in regard to the nature of the present perception.

222
00:25:28,597 --> 00:25:33,741
[SPEAKER_00]: And you could see that even, even the very beginning, it was about the negative.

223
00:25:35,070 --> 00:25:40,674
[SPEAKER_00]: When the Buddha was in Megara's mother's palace, he wasn't saying, look at this palace, look at the floor, look at the post.

224
00:25:40,714 --> 00:25:40,814
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

225
00:25:40,834 --> 00:25:42,695
[SPEAKER_00]: He was talking about things that are not there.

226
00:25:44,476 --> 00:25:45,957
[SPEAKER_00]: So, from there, you go higher.

227
00:25:47,578 --> 00:25:49,560
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you realize, okay, there are things that are there.

228
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:51,381
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where the mind is established upon.

229
00:25:51,761 --> 00:25:52,602
[SPEAKER_00]: But then, you go further.

230
00:25:52,622 --> 00:25:53,502
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what else is there?

231
00:25:54,043 --> 00:25:55,644
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that place is in the forest.

232
00:25:56,184 --> 00:26:01,588
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the mind can then be established upon the forest, even without you having to go and stare at the trees and mossy rocks and so on.

233
00:26:04,232 --> 00:26:08,459
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, what else is there, based on things that are not there?

234
00:26:08,499 --> 00:26:12,225
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the understanding of the peripheral, and that's the definition of proper mindfulness.

235
00:26:13,532 --> 00:26:17,493
[SPEAKER_00]: whereby what you are attending, you discern the peripheral in regard to it.

236
00:26:18,053 --> 00:26:21,734
[SPEAKER_00]: And the ultimate peripheral is the presence of the phenomenon, the infinite consciousness.

237
00:26:22,194 --> 00:26:27,495
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, even the greater peripheral than that, it would be even that place of neither perception or no perception.

238
00:26:27,935 --> 00:26:34,757
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's, that's, that's now you bringing back onto yourself, so to, so to develop the full understanding.

239
00:26:34,797 --> 00:26:38,598
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, when even that perception ceases in the signless establishment of the mind,

240
00:26:39,487 --> 00:26:41,552
[SPEAKER_00]: No more signs means no more peripheral.

241
00:26:41,772 --> 00:26:43,676
[SPEAKER_00]: Means you have reached the ultimate peripheral.

242
00:26:43,957 --> 00:26:44,598
[SPEAKER_00]: Sign-less.

243
00:26:45,380 --> 00:26:47,204
[SPEAKER_00]: Because all the signs are peripherally.

244
00:26:48,953 --> 00:26:50,974
[SPEAKER_00]: That's just how the nature of a sign works.

245
00:26:51,794 --> 00:27:03,520
[SPEAKER_00]: So, once the mind has reached that complete cessation, as in there is no further to go in that structure, and that's, by the way, the Sutta Majjhima 111, where Sariputta, one by one, when he would think, is there higher?

246
00:27:03,540 --> 00:27:03,960
[SPEAKER_00]: There is.

247
00:27:04,221 --> 00:27:11,584
[SPEAKER_00]: From one goes to the other one, to the other one, and he fully penetrates and understands the entire structure of the experience from the inside, of course.

248
00:27:11,684 --> 00:27:12,785
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't step outside of it.

249
00:27:13,445 --> 00:27:21,931
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he understands, okay, this is it, this is the ultimate, there is no higher than this, the signless understanding, the signless establishment of the mind.

250
00:27:24,593 --> 00:27:25,334
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh...

251
00:27:25,963 --> 00:27:34,009
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in this case, the monk has fully understood all the more general phenomena in regard to that which is present in front of him.

252
00:27:34,649 --> 00:27:47,699
[SPEAKER_00]: And because of that, he realizes that whatever taint, whatever anxiety, whatever disturbance based on taint of sensuality, taint of being, taint of ignorance, cannot arise for him because he's free from those taints.

253
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:59,223
[SPEAKER_00]: And then he realized that only disturbance based upon the sixth domain, dependent upon this very body, with life as condition, that's any disturbance he still has left.

254
00:27:59,583 --> 00:28:01,264
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the disturbance for an arahant.

255
00:28:01,644 --> 00:28:04,925
[SPEAKER_00]: For as long as his body is still alive, that body can be disturbed.

256
00:28:05,585 --> 00:28:08,126
[SPEAKER_00]: But none of that can cause suffering or bother him anymore.

257
00:28:08,166 --> 00:28:10,187
[SPEAKER_00]: So all the symptoms of avijja have ceased.

258
00:28:15,162 --> 00:28:21,667
[SPEAKER_00]: Having, he understands, having arrived at this perception, it is empty of the taint of being, empty of taint of sensuality, taint of being and taint of ignorance.

259
00:28:22,148 --> 00:28:28,132
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands there is only this non-emptiness, namely the six domains dependent on this very body with life as condition.

260
00:28:29,754 --> 00:28:33,717
[SPEAKER_00]: Thus, on account of whatever is not there, he sees it as it is empty.

261
00:28:34,418 --> 00:28:38,141
[SPEAKER_00]: And whatever remains, he understands it, this is present.

262
00:28:39,061 --> 00:28:44,826
[SPEAKER_00]: And in this way and under, there is this authentic, undistorted, clear entry into the emptiness which is the best with nothing higher.

263
00:28:47,872 --> 00:28:58,787
[SPEAKER_00]: Ānanda, whatever ascetics and brāhmaṇas in the past entered upon and dwelled in the clear emptiness, which is the best, with nothing higher, all of them entered upon and dwell in this very clear emptiness, which is the best, with nothing higher.

264
00:28:58,807 --> 00:28:59,328
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what I mean.

265
00:28:59,388 --> 00:29:00,149
[SPEAKER_00]: It's structural.

266
00:29:00,169 --> 00:29:04,335
[SPEAKER_00]: It means the human experience, the experience of the five aggregates, for that matter.

267
00:29:05,431 --> 00:29:10,954
[SPEAKER_00]: A certain order, and this is the order that one... the one with understanding develops and understands.

268
00:29:11,535 --> 00:29:18,199
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why the Buddha says, whoever has done this in the past, eons ago, and whoever will do it in the future, will do it in this manner.

269
00:29:19,140 --> 00:29:19,840
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the structure.

270
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,701
[SPEAKER_00]: It's... it's not... it's not a matter of choice.

271
00:29:22,982 --> 00:29:27,625
[SPEAKER_00]: With nothing higher, all of them enter upon and dwell in this very clear emptiness, which is the best.

272
00:29:27,645 --> 00:29:32,308
[SPEAKER_00]: And Ananda, whatever I said in the Brahmins, in the future will enter upon and dwell in the clear emptiness, which is the best.

273
00:29:33,100 --> 00:29:34,761
[SPEAKER_00]: And same goes for the ones that do it right now.

274
00:29:34,781 --> 00:29:37,383
[SPEAKER_00]: This is what the Blessed One said.

275
00:29:37,403 --> 00:29:41,866
[SPEAKER_00]: Please, the Venerable Ananda, enlighten in the words of the Blessed One.

276
00:29:59,948 --> 00:30:10,059
[SPEAKER_00]: So, in terms of practical development of what's been discussed in this sutta, physical seclusion is necessary, obviously.

277
00:30:10,159 --> 00:30:13,242
[SPEAKER_00]: Absence of other people, absence of the perceptions of the village.

278
00:30:15,464 --> 00:30:18,608
[SPEAKER_00]: So, ideally, places like forests,

279
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:25,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Mountains, where you would be actually physically removed from other people.

280
00:30:26,647 --> 00:30:36,336
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you don't, as I said during the reading, you don't have to go around looking at things and telling yourself you're in the forest, because you are in the forest.

281
00:30:38,619 --> 00:30:41,662
[SPEAKER_00]: So, peripherally, you will be discerning things that are absent.

282
00:30:43,384 --> 00:30:48,647
[SPEAKER_00]: Until then, the mind settles in the perceptions of the forest, the mood of the experience of the forest.

283
00:30:49,028 --> 00:30:54,791
[SPEAKER_00]: And the only way to develop a mood of the experience of the forest is to go and be in the forest, or be alone.

284
00:30:57,153 --> 00:31:07,019
[SPEAKER_00]: But there has to be some distance between you and other people, at least temporarily, for the duration of that practice.

285
00:31:09,221 --> 00:31:12,283
[SPEAKER_00]: So, eh... the perceptions of the forest

286
00:31:13,509 --> 00:31:14,370
[SPEAKER_00]: are in the background.

287
00:31:15,611 --> 00:31:20,635
[SPEAKER_00]: The tree in front of you, the big rock in front of you, the cave next to you, those things are not the forest.

288
00:31:20,795 --> 00:31:21,636
[SPEAKER_00]: They're in the forest.

289
00:31:22,216 --> 00:31:23,137
[SPEAKER_00]: And you're there with them.

290
00:31:23,417 --> 00:31:24,498
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you are in the forest.

291
00:31:25,159 --> 00:31:33,786
[SPEAKER_00]: So, as I said, you don't need to keep reminding yourself and looking at various objects in front of you and touching, touching, moving, looking, touching, whatever.

292
00:31:34,646 --> 00:31:35,127
[SPEAKER_00]: They're there.

293
00:31:35,947 --> 00:31:37,989
[SPEAKER_00]: And you are in that forest together with them.

294
00:31:38,910 --> 00:31:41,612
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you discern the presence of the forest peripherally.

295
00:31:43,790 --> 00:31:48,492
[SPEAKER_00]: Being properly mindful of it.

296
00:31:50,793 --> 00:31:54,534
[SPEAKER_00]: You discern it as something that you partake in.

297
00:31:55,254 --> 00:31:56,355
[SPEAKER_00]: You are now in that forest.

298
00:31:56,755 --> 00:31:59,216
[SPEAKER_00]: You are partaking in that more general perception.

299
00:31:59,596 --> 00:32:01,777
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how the mind gets established upon that.

300
00:32:02,317 --> 00:32:03,337
[SPEAKER_00]: And you would see the difference.

301
00:32:03,417 --> 00:32:10,480
[SPEAKER_00]: Just spend two or three days secluded from people, going back among people, going back into the village or a town.

302
00:32:11,769 --> 00:32:12,790
[SPEAKER_00]: You will see the difference.

303
00:32:13,251 --> 00:32:16,254
[SPEAKER_00]: You will see how different it is, how different the situation becomes.

304
00:32:16,734 --> 00:32:25,944
[SPEAKER_00]: But the point here is to maintain your establishment of your mind through that clarity of discernment.

305
00:32:26,044 --> 00:32:27,606
[SPEAKER_00]: Maintain it upon the forest.

306
00:32:28,207 --> 00:32:30,869
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, say you have to go to the town or the village.

307
00:32:33,079 --> 00:32:47,727
[SPEAKER_00]: But you, even when you do, even when you're in the middle of the town square, you still see yourself as belonging to the forest, as belonging to the greater perception than all these things that are around you, that are obviously more inferior to it.

308
00:32:47,767 --> 00:32:49,448
[SPEAKER_00]: Villages are inferior to the forests.

309
00:32:50,365 --> 00:32:53,786
[SPEAKER_00]: Inhabited areas are inferior to the non-inhabited areas.

310
00:32:54,526 --> 00:33:00,387
[SPEAKER_00]: So you see yourself pertaining, partaking in, being part of the greater forest.

311
00:33:01,007 --> 00:33:18,871
[SPEAKER_00]: And for as long as you maintain that mood, peripherally, you're mindful of it, you allow it to endure, you can spend long time among people, and in the towns, and villages, and still partake to the forest.

312
00:33:24,230 --> 00:33:31,075
[SPEAKER_00]: But, of course, if you see yourself as partaking to the forest, you wouldn't want to be lingering around the inhabited areas, unless you have to.

313
00:33:31,555 --> 00:33:37,559
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you would go when you have to, do things that you have to, but then go back to that which is greater.

314
00:33:37,920 --> 00:33:40,081
[SPEAKER_00]: The perception of the forest, that is empty of those things.

315
00:33:40,482 --> 00:33:46,406
[SPEAKER_00]: So, even when you would be among those things, you're dwelling in the emptiness of those things, because the mind is established upon a more general mood.

316
00:33:47,457 --> 00:33:53,759
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, same, when you get used to dwelling in the forest, when you see yourself partaking in the forest, being part of the forest, go even higher.

317
00:33:54,700 --> 00:34:01,582
[SPEAKER_00]: Start discerning the presence of the phenomenon of Earth, peripherally, within which the forest is, within which you are.

318
00:34:03,763 --> 00:34:11,566
[SPEAKER_00]: So, now, wherever you are, whether it's a forest, town, mountain, island, doesn't matter, you are within the perception of the Earth.

319
00:34:12,126 --> 00:34:13,467
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you could see, eh...

320
00:34:14,305 --> 00:34:18,208
[SPEAKER_00]: Say, the perception of the forest upon which your mood depends, upon which your situation has been developed.

321
00:34:18,589 --> 00:34:22,252
[SPEAKER_00]: Say, there's a massive flood, earthquake, fire, everything gets destroyed.

322
00:34:22,792 --> 00:34:26,815
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what means disturbance upon the perception of the forest can still arise.

323
00:34:27,496 --> 00:34:37,384
[SPEAKER_00]: But, unless something destroys the entire planet Earth, eh... the mind that's established upon the general perception of the Earth cannot be disturbed then by anything.

324
00:34:38,285 --> 00:34:40,967
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's that's the similar to the practice of Earth Casino.

325
00:34:42,493 --> 00:34:47,598
[SPEAKER_00]: Where the mind gets established upon it, and then the Buddha said, everything inferior to it, will not bother you.

326
00:34:49,940 --> 00:34:56,326
[SPEAKER_00]: But the only way to establish this, is to start discerning it, on the level of that which is present.

327
00:34:56,587 --> 00:34:58,889
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what the sutta we just read said.

328
00:34:59,629 --> 00:35:01,852
[SPEAKER_00]: Said, he understands, this is what's present.

329
00:35:03,013 --> 00:35:04,294
[SPEAKER_00]: This is present in front of me.

330
00:35:06,071 --> 00:35:12,617
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the peripheral... the peripheral... the peripheral mindfulness of the mood in the forest is what's present.

331
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:14,198
[SPEAKER_00]: It's what's my situation.

332
00:35:15,719 --> 00:35:26,248
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, the peripheral... the mind established upon the peripheral discernment of the... of the... of the domain, of the perception of the earth, is what my situation is in.

333
00:35:26,928 --> 00:35:31,252
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you can go further to the infinite space, the infinite consciousness and so on.

334
00:35:32,353 --> 00:35:34,455
[SPEAKER_00]: But even... even just the perception of the earth,

335
00:35:35,318 --> 00:35:53,061
[SPEAKER_00]: is more than enough, in terms of its generality, in terms of its structural capacity, to allow the understanding and the cessation of any greed, aversion, delusion, lust, towards things that are inferior to it.

336
00:35:54,162 --> 00:35:57,423
[SPEAKER_00]: But, one needs to start dwelling in it.

337
00:35:57,484 --> 00:35:58,244
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not a theory.

338
00:35:58,264 --> 00:35:59,304
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not an abstract thought.

339
00:35:59,344 --> 00:36:00,925
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to see yourself partaking.

340
00:36:00,945 --> 00:36:06,868
[SPEAKER_00]: You need to see yourself in your being as something that partakes to that level of that general perception.

341
00:36:06,908 --> 00:36:07,408
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what it is.

342
00:36:07,448 --> 00:36:08,449
[SPEAKER_00]: He's clear about.

343
00:36:08,549 --> 00:36:09,649
[SPEAKER_00]: He's established on it.

344
00:36:09,689 --> 00:36:10,569
[SPEAKER_00]: He remains in it.

345
00:36:10,630 --> 00:36:11,390
[SPEAKER_00]: He dwells in it.

346
00:36:13,691 --> 00:36:17,993
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that takes repetitive effort and obviously, it takes... requires seclusion.

347
00:36:19,213 --> 00:36:32,621
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why the Buddha could not have, sort of, encouraged too much monks and those interested in practice to go and develop physical... dwell in physical seclusion, because it all comes from it.

348
00:36:32,661 --> 00:36:41,687
[SPEAKER_00]: And there is that another sutta, similar on emptiness, where the monk goes into the empty forest, root of a tree, empty cave, empty dwelling and says, this place is empty of others.

349
00:36:42,933 --> 00:36:55,164
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's his starting point, again, to go back into discerning one by one this structure of the arisen situation, of that which is present, which is just another way of saying the establishment of the mind.

350
00:36:55,864 --> 00:37:04,332
[SPEAKER_00]: And jhānas work in the same way, just they're more specific in terms of the domain of sensuality, being surmounted and so on, and maybe we can talk about it on a different occasion.

351
00:37:05,192 --> 00:37:07,895
[SPEAKER_00]: But in this case, physical seclusion,

352
00:37:09,278 --> 00:37:25,162
[SPEAKER_00]: Dwelling in that which is superior to the inhabited life, inhabited areas, crowded areas, that's how these perceptions begin to be discerned peripherally, and that's how the mind can get established upon them.

353
00:37:27,063 --> 00:37:32,384
[SPEAKER_00]: So, just one more thing to point out, that the more general perception of Earth

354
00:37:36,670 --> 00:37:47,079
[SPEAKER_00]: is established upon, or rather through, the perceptions of the mood of the forest, the mood of the situation of being in the forest.

355
00:37:48,941 --> 00:37:55,667
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything that doesn't go in that order, like one after the other, as in the perception of earth after,

356
00:37:56,640 --> 00:37:59,462
[SPEAKER_00]: The perception of the mood of the forest, it will be abstract.

357
00:38:00,082 --> 00:38:03,185
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if it doesn't follow the right order, it's going to be on the level of abstraction.

358
00:38:03,385 --> 00:38:12,551
[SPEAKER_00]: Abstraction, which means there won't be mindfulness properly established and mind will not be established upon the one-pointedness of that more general perception.

359
00:38:13,092 --> 00:38:25,701
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if a person wants to discern the perceptions of Earth, they need to be done within or on the basis or through the basis of the of the mood of being in the forest.

360
00:38:26,799 --> 00:38:30,142
[SPEAKER_00]: The mood of being part of the forest, the mood of being the forest.

361
00:38:31,523 --> 00:38:38,210
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that then, you start refining that very mood, perception of the mood of being the forest, and that's where the perception of earth is found.

